        "custom_liquid": "<highlight class=\"top-highlight\">Shilajit tastes different from anything your palate expects. An original shilajit is blackish to brownish in color, smells like cow’s urine, and is tar-like and would dissolve in water in the form of continuous strands. It has an earthy taste with a metallic tang.</highlight>\n<p>With this basic understanding of Shilajit, it is now time to proceed to its origin story in the rocks of the high altitudes, the history that surrounds it, its rich composition, its harvesting process-from rocks to your table, and the numerous health benefits that continue to be discovered today.</p>\n\n<style>\n.top-highlight{\nmargin-bottom:3.2rem;\n}\n.custom-html{\nmargin-bottom:11rem;\n}\n.main-wrapper{\nmargin-top:7rem;}\n.main__icon{\nmargin:-1.2% 0;\n}\n@media(max-width:768px){\n.main__icon{\nmargin: -20px 0;\n}\n.main-wrapper{\n  margin-top:40px;\nmargin-bottom:56px;\n}\n.custom-html{\nmargin-bottom:40px;\n}\n}\n</style>"
